>> title: Birria de Res, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, chiles, mexican, braise, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: birria-de-res
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: birria, birria tacos, taco de birria, quesabirria, red taco, slow cooker birria, crockpot birria de res
>> pairs-with: corn-tortillas, salsa-roja
>> servings: 8
>> time: 8 hr 25 min
>> slack: forgiving — beef this fatty is shreddable at seven hours and better at nine; the only thing that spoils is the consomé, and that is a spoon lifting the fat off, not a clock
>> step.2: toast the chiles 5 min, dry skillet
>> step.3: blend to an adobo
>> step.4: strain
>> step.5: slow cook on low, 8 hr
>> step.6: lift the fat, separate the consomé

Nothing is browned here, and the oven version does not brown it either: birria's colour and depth come out of the chile adobo, not out of a sear. So this is a genuine one-load dish — the skillet is used for five minutes of dry-toasting chiles and then washed. The adobo goes in at two and a half cups where the oven takes four, because the pot gives nothing back to the air all day.

Toast @dried guajillo chiles{6}(stemmed and seeded), @dried ancho chiles{3}(stemmed and seeded) in a dry #skillet{} for ~toast{5%min}, until they smell of raisins and before they smell of ash.

Blend @&(~1)toasted chiles{} with @white onion{1%large}(quartered), @garlic{5%cloves}, @cider vinegar{3%Tbs}, @ground cumin{1%tsp}, @Mexican oregano{1%tsp}, @cinnamon stick{1}, @whole cloves{4}, @bay leaves{2}, @black peppercorns{1%tsp}, @water{2 1/2%cup}(590 mL; hot).

Strain @&(~1)adobo{} through a #fine-mesh sieve{}, pressing the solids to get everything through but the skins.

Slow cook @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 3-in pieces), @beef short ribs{1%lb}(450 g), @kosher salt{1%Tbs} under @&(~1)strained adobo{} in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on and left alone.

Lift the fat from @&(~1)birria{} with a ladle and keep it: the red fat on top is what fries the tortilla, the meat is shredded back into a little of the sauce, and the rest of the liquid is the consomé that goes out in a cup beside it.
